# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true by default, which materialises every
# file with CRLF on clone. Prettier's endOfLine default is "lf", so without this
# a fresh Windows clone fails `npm run verify` at format:check before the
# scaffold has changed a single line — see the Foundation Fix Log, 2026-07-30.
#
# Normalise to LF in the index and check out LF on every platform regardless of
# the user's core.autocrlf. Binaries (icons, fonts) are auto-detected by
# text=auto and left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
